For the latest news, visit the SparForte web site.

Objective: Fixes before foundation for value meta labels (Phase 2)

Known Issues

Ubuntu 26.04: PCRE2 is not supported.

CHANGES SINCE 3.0

1. Fix: In files.is_execute/is_execute file, the group execute permission is now checked.

2. Fix: In files.is_readable and other functions that check readability, in edge cases where the kernel getlogin() fails and, in turn, group_member() fails, the read access checks fall back to checking the simple file gid againt the user's effective gid.  Comments also fixed in c_os.c.

3. Change: when a hash-able command (e.g. "foo") is not found but a file exists without executable permission, an error message describes this condition rather than describing it as not found. When a command path (e.g. "/bin/foo") cannot be run when the file exists without executable permission, an error describes this condition rather than describing it as not found.

4. pragma annotate( generator ) for automation generated source code as per Linux kernel standards.

5. Fix: certain edge cases in subprogram parameter names like names already in use, duplicate parameter names, a parameter with the name of the subprogram should now work correctly.

6. Fix: most declarations now include the declaration location for error messages (such as enum type items, for example).

7. New: constant values are checked for placeholder values in testing and maintenance modes.

8. Fix: -C / --coding disables the default testing mode flag instead of enabling both.

9. Fix: case statments can now test array elements as well as scalar variables.

10. Fix: using an parent meta tag to declare a child tag no longer has an unreferenced error.

11. Change: general cleanup of provision script.  Support for os-release file when detecting your O/S.

12. Fix: no bug report is displayed if a forked process fails (e.g. bad bang path).

13. Fix: Sturges formula, reverse of ln2/ln10 constants fixed in parser_numerics.

14. Change: added GNU readline version 9 detection to configure script.

15. Change: strings.is_fixed allows a leading space or minus sign.

16. Fix: when cleanup up background processes, fixed a issue where the cleanup could be delayed by one command line.

17. Fix: when parsing command paths for the command hash table, ~ is replaced with the value of HOME rather than the current working directory.

18. Fix: arrays.length correctly returns zero for any first bound larger than the last bound on an array type or subtype.

19. Fix: besides arrays of 1..0, any first bound greater than a last bound will  be treated as empty by the array package sort functions.

20. Change: added colour output for HTML messages corresponding to the console colours that appear when --colour/--color is used.  The HTML colours remain even if --colour/--color is not used.

21. Fix: in the unusual case of a SparForte message with a 1-character string, it should capitalize without an exception (though there are currently no strings this short).

22. Fix: documentation review and cleanup of spelling, grammar, structure.  Package documentation cross-referenced with source code.

23. Fix: perl_match tests moved to third-party tests.

24. New: Ubuntu 26.04 support.

25. Fix: arrays.shuffle modified slightly to better fit classic Fisher-Yates method.

26. Fix: The btree_io package has some error messages corrected.

27. Fix: More thorough exception handling on btree_io/hash_io open and create.

28. Fix: Missing meta tag check on URL encode.

29. Fix: command_line.environment.environment_value has a better error message when the position is out-of-range.

30. Fix: The btree_io and hash_io support path separators besides UNIX "/".

31. Fix: Spelling of directory_operations.absolute_dir_name_dir corrected.

32. Fix: Fixed swapped parameters for doubly_linked_lists.assign and move.

33. Change: doubly_linked_lists.assemble/disassemble now use O/S-specific EOL characters rather than an ASCII.LF.

34. Fix: removed debugging "raise" from enums.pos.

35. Fix: enum.succ returns built-in enumerated items as well as user-defined ones.

36. Fix: gnat.cgi fixed.

37. Fix: gnat.crc32.get_value performs the final XOR.

38. Fix: l10n.t_fmt_ampm returns results of t_fmt_ampm instead of the pm string. era_t_fmt now returns era_t_fmt instead of era_d_fmt.

39. Fix: removed memory leak when a script ends without clearing the memcache/memcache.highread servers.

40. Fix: searching the lists of memcache/memcache.highread cluster servers corrected (= vs. >= in the search).

41. Fix: mysql.schema and mysqlm.schema fixed to do a "select" rather than "show" query.

42. Fix: sound package no longer restarts gstreamer if reinitialized more than once.

43. Fix: text_io is_open fixed for current_error.

44. Fix: text_io close and delete will not close/delete current output or current error.

45. Fix: units.sqmiles2sqkm was documented was missing but now implemented.

46. Fix: units package documentation dry and liquid ounces corrected to dry and liquid gallons.

47. Fix: completed TODO for vectors package find/reverse_find memory leak.

48. Fix: signal action for SA_RESTART fag no longer assumes an initial value of zero.

